/*!

\page SimpleApi QCAD Simple API

The QCAD Simple API is a small set of global ECMAScript functions that
simplify common tasks such as adding, querying and modifying entities.
It is mainly designed for use in the script shell (Misc > Development >
Script Shell) and for short scripts, but it can also be used from any
script or plugin. The complete function reference is available in the
module \ref ecma_simple.

\section simple_usage Usage

In the script shell, the Simple API is available directly. In scripts,
include the file simple.js:

\code
include("simple.js");

addLine(0,0, 100,100);
var c = addCircle([50,50], 25);
trim(c, [75,50], [10,10]);
\endcode

The functions operate on the current document of the QCAD main window.
Use \ref startTransaction to apply a series of calls as one transaction
(one undo step) or to redirect calls to an off-screen document
(\ref createDocument, \ref createDocumentInterface).

\section simple_refs Entity References

Functions that take an entity accept the entity in various forms.
This applies to all modification functions (\ref trim, \ref round,
\ref offset, \ref move, ...) as well as to the query functions
\ref getEntity and \ref getShape:

<table>
<tr><th>Form</th><th>Example</th><th>Meaning</th></tr>
<tr><td>Entity ID</td><td><tt>trim(1234, 1235)</tt></td>
<td>The entity with the given ID in the current document.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Entity object (REntity)</td><td><tt>var l = addLine(0,0, 10,0); move(l, [0,5]);</tt></td>
<td>The entity is looked up by its ID in the current document. Entities returned by
the add functions (\ref addLine, \ref addCircle, ...) can be passed directly.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Shape (RShape)</td><td><tt>var s = new RLine(0,0, 10,0); offset(s, 1);</tt></td>
<td>The operation is applied to the shape only, the drawing is not changed.
Transformations (\ref move, \ref rotate, \ref scale, \ref mirror, \ref lengthen,
\ref reverse) modify the shape in place. All other functions return the resulting
shapes as an array and leave the given shapes unchanged.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Position (RVector or [x,y])</td><td><tt>trim([2,0], [5,3])</tt></td>
<td>The entity closest to the given position in the drawing. The position also
serves as click position (see below).</td></tr>
</table>

Positions can always be given as RVector or as array <tt>[x,y]</tt>. Most functions
also accept positions as two separate numbers (<tt>addLine(0,0, 100,100)</tt>).

\subsection simple_clickpos Click Positions

Some operations depend on where an entity was 'clicked': trimming keeps the part
of the entity at the click position, rounding and beveling round the ends of the
entities that are closest to the click positions, offsetting creates the parallel
on the side of the click position.

A click position may follow every entity reference that is not itself a position:

\code
trim(line1, [8,0], line2, [5,3])    // explicit click positions
trim([8,0], [5,3])                  // positions as references: same result
trim(line1, line2)                  // no click positions: middle points are used
\endcode

If no click position is given, the middle point of the entity is used.

\section simple_results Return Values

- Creation functions return the added entity (with a valid ID unless called
  within a transaction).
- Transformations (\ref move, \ref rotate, \ref scale, \ref mirror,
  \ref lengthen, \ref reverse) return the modified entity.
- Other modification functions (\ref trim, \ref round, \ref bevel, \ref offset,
  \ref breakOut, \ref divide, \ref explode, \ref stretch) return the RTransaction
  created by the operation or undefined when called within a transaction
  (see \ref startTransaction) or if the operation failed. Failures are reported
  with \ref warning.
- If only shapes are passed, the resulting shapes are returned as an array.

\section simple_functions Function Overview

\subsection simple_functions_doc Documents and Application

<table>
<tr><td>\ref getMainWindow</td><td>Main application window.</td></tr>
<tr><td>\ref getDocumentInterface</td><td>Current document interface.</td></tr>
<tr><td>\ref getDocument</td><td>Current document.</td></tr>
<tr><td>\ref getGraphicsView</td><td>Current graphics view.</td></tr>
<tr><td>\ref createDocument</td><td>Creates an off-screen document.</td></tr>
<tr><td>\ref createDocumentInterface</td><td>Creates an off-screen document interface.</td></tr>
<tr><td>\ref disableInput, \ref enableInput, \ref isInputEnabled</td><td>Block user input during long operations.</td></tr>
<tr><td>\ref update</td><td>Keeps the user interface up to date during long operations.</td></tr>
<tr><td>\ref sleep</td><td>Sleeps for the given number of milliseconds.</td></tr>
<tr><td>\ref warning</td><td>Prints a warning.</td></tr>
</table>

\subsection simple_functions_create Creation

<table>
<tr><td>\ref addPoint, \ref addLine, \ref addXLine, \ref addArc, \ref addCircle, \ref addEllipse,
\ref addPolyline, \ref addSpline, \ref addSimpleText, \ref addSolid</td><td>Add entities to the drawing.</td></tr>
<tr><td>\ref addShape, \ref addShapes, \ref addEntity, \ref addObject</td><td>Add shapes, entities or other objects (layers, blocks, ...).</td></tr>
<tr><td>\ref addLayer, \ref hasLayer, \ref setCurrentLayer</td><td>Layers.</td></tr>
<tr><td>\ref setCurrentColor</td><td>Color of newly added entities.</td></tr>
<tr><td>\ref deleteObject</td><td>Deletes an object.</td></tr>
</table>

\subsection simple_functions_info Information and Queries

<table>
<tr><td>\ref getEntity</td><td>Entity for an entity ID, entity object or position.</td></tr>
<tr><td>\ref getShape</td><td>Shape for an entity reference or shape.</td></tr>
<tr><td>\ref getClosestEntity</td><td>Entity closest to a position.</td></tr>
<tr><td>\ref getEntityShape</td><td>Shape of an entity (closest sub shape for complex entities).</td></tr>
<tr><td>\ref getIntersectionPoints</td><td>Intersection points between two entities or shapes.</td></tr>
<tr><td>\ref isPosition, \ref toVector</td><td>Position helpers (RVector or [x,y]).</td></tr>
</table>

\subsection simple_functions_modify Modification

<table>
<tr><td>\ref move, \ref rotate, \ref scale, \ref mirror</td><td>Transformations.</td></tr>
<tr><td>\ref trim, \ref trimBoth</td><td>Trim one or both entities to each other (or extend them).</td></tr>
<tr><td>\ref lengthen</td><td>Lengthen or shorten an entity at its start or end.</td></tr>
<tr><td>\ref breakOut</td><td>Remove the segment between the closest intersections.</td></tr>
<tr><td>\ref autoTrim</td><td>Keep only the segment between the closest intersections.</td></tr>
<tr><td>\ref divide</td><td>Divide an entity at one or two positions.</td></tr>
<tr><td>\ref round</td><td>Round a corner (fillet).</td></tr>
<tr><td>\ref bevel, \ref chamfer</td><td>Bevel a corner (chamfer).</td></tr>
<tr><td>\ref offset</td><td>Create parallels / concentric copies.</td></tr>
<tr><td>\ref reverse</td><td>Reverse the direction of an entity.</td></tr>
<tr><td>\ref explode</td><td>Explode an entity into its components.</td></tr>
<tr><td>\ref stretch</td><td>Stretch the entities in an area.</td></tr>
<tr><td>\ref deleteEntity</td><td>Delete an entity.</td></tr>
<tr><td>\ref paste</td><td>Paste a document into another document.</td></tr>
</table>

\subsection simple_functions_transaction Transactions

<table>
<tr><td>\ref startTransaction, \ref endTransaction</td><td>Group calls into one transaction (one undo step) or
apply them to an off-screen document.</td></tr>
<tr><td>\ref getTransactionDocument, \ref getTransactionDocumentInterface</td><td>Document the current transaction applies to.</td></tr>
<tr><td>\ref getOperation</td><td>Operation of the current transaction (for advanced use).</td></tr>
</table>

\subsection simple_functions_view View

<table>
<tr><td>\ref autoZoom</td><td>Auto zoom.</td></tr>
<tr><td>\ref zoomTo</td><td>Zoom to an entity, box or position.</td></tr>
</table>

\subsection simple_functions_input User Input

<table>
<tr><td>\ref getInt, \ref getDouble, \ref getText, \ref getItem</td><td>Input dialogs.</td></tr>
</table>

\section simple_examples Examples

Draw a rectangle from four lines and round its corners:

\code
startTransaction();
var l1 = addLine(0,0, 100,0);
var l2 = addLine(100,0, 100,50);
var l3 = addLine(100,50, 0,50);
var l4 = addLine(0,50, 0,0);
endTransaction();

round(l1, l2, 10);
round(l2, l3, 10);
round(l3, l4, 10);
round(l4, l1, 10);
\endcode

Trim a line to a circle, keeping the part at the click position:

\code
var line = addLine(0,0, 100,0);
var circle = addCircle([50,0], 20);
trim(line, [10,0], circle);          // keeps the part from (0,0) to (30,0)
\endcode

Use positions only (e.g. with coordinates taken from the drawing):

\code
trimBoth([10,0], [50,30]);           // trim the entities at these positions to each other
breakOut([60,5]);                    // remove the segment around (60,5)
offset([50,0], 5, 3);                // three parallels on both sides of the entity at (50,0)
bevel([10,0], [100,20], 5);          // chamfer the corner between the entities at these positions
\endcode

Work with shapes without changing the drawing:

\code
var s1 = new RLine(0,0, 10,0);
var s2 = new RLine(10,0, 10,10);
var res = round(s1, s2, 2);          // [trimmed s1, RArc, trimmed s2]
addShapes(res);
\endcode

Apply a series of modifications as a single undo step or to an off-screen document:

\code
var di = createDocumentInterface();
startTransaction(di);
var a = addLine(0,0, 10,0);
var b = addLine(5,-5, 5,5);
trim(a, [8,0], b);
endTransaction();
di.exportFile("/tmp/out.dxf", "R27 (2013) DXF");
\endcode

<p>&nbsp;</p>

*/
